d inputs; this judgment does not verify the source contracts or source fidelity.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0\",\"/inputs/1\",\"/inference/inputs\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"At S003 the map p is declared with domain F, whereas M004 requires f:X→Y and then applies it to a set A⊆X. The inequality for points of F does not by itself provide the required function on all of X. First unsupported application: M004's hypothesis (X=E×[0,1], A=F) is not established by the declaration of p.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/applications/3/bindings\",\"/inputs/3/source_contract/signature\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The listed M004 is identifiable as the intended dependency, but its required domain-level Lipschitz map is not established by the prose. The application record cannot add that missing fact.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/applications/3\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"S001 and S002 attempt the upper and positive-D lower bounds, respectively, but the stated D=0 lower-bound route has the M004 applicability defect, so the whole claimed equality is not established by this argument.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The proof text treats the D=0 and D>0 cases as branches and the variables used in the identified M004 application do not escape a temporary witness scope. This does not resolve the domain mismatch.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/locals/11\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"M004's stated signature requires f:X→Y. The binding declares p:F→[0,1] only; its pointwise distance estimate covers points in F, not arbitrary points of X. Other source applicability checks are not independently certified by this packet-only review.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/applications/3/bindings\",\"/inputs/3/source_contract/signature\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The input and output propositions relevant to the identified failure are stated in full enough to understand the intended sets and dimension conclusion without producer proofs. This is not a source-fidelity judgment.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/output/statement\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The actual map p in S003 has a declared domain F, but the M004 application treats it as a map on X=E×[0,1]. The declarations do not close that object/domain mismatch.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/applications/3/bindings\",\"/inference/locals/11\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The factual use of M004 at S003 requires a whole-ambient-space Lipschitz map; the prose supplies only a map whose declared domain is F. No direct input or earlier local proof supplies the missing domain extension.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/applications/3\",\"/inference/locals/11\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"I read packet.json in full in this context and used only that packet as mathematical task material, along with the declared Yui rules. The available interaction does not provide independent carrier/execution evidence, so I cannot attest that this was an authenticated fresh-carrier replay. I make no runtime or identity claim.\",\"locations\":[\"/packet_sha256\",\"/warning\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"premises\":\"The prose defines p:F→[0,1] and verifies its Lipschitz inequality for points in F; M004 has signature f:X→Y and applies dimension to f '' A for A⊆X.\",\"conclusion\":\"dim_H([0,1])≤dim_H(F) by M004.\",\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"reason\":\"The required map on X=E×[0,1] is not d